Subject: A pass recorded both ways is recorded for tiles alone once tiles are certain

Since gpu-pass a pass that may be tiled is recorded for tiles and for sysmem, and closePass chooses by what the
pass turned out to hold (render::gmemWorth). CoreAnimation's main pass -- a hundred draws and more, tiled every
frame -- was so written twice from its first draw to its last, the sysmem words thrown away.

What gmemWorth weighs only grows as draws are added: the draws, the attachments they touch, whether one reads its
target; and no pass loads and stores more than every attachment it has. So the choice is known to be tiles, whatever
is still to come, from the draw at which
- the pass has kGmemFewDraws draws and one of them reads its target, or
- draws * the bytes touched so far >= the bar * the bytes of every attachment (which bounds gmemWorth's
  bar * (11 (loaded + stored) - 10 cleared) <= draws * 22 touched), or
- with kGmemByDrawsAlone, the draws reach the bar.
From that draw the sysmem side is let go: the tiles' head goes onto the stream then, as closePass would have put it,
and the draws after are written once. closePass notes the pass as it would have (OpenPass::tiledEarly: a heavy one
of its kind, below the bar or not).

Two things differ from before, and nothing else:
- a draw that reads its target no longer takes a second table for the sysmem side once the choice is made, so the
  tables after it lie elsewhere: the golden sums of what the loads name are what they were, the stream sums of the
  scenes with fetches in tiled passes change by those addresses (B, Q, and the tests that draw so);
- a draw that cannot be tiled arriving after the choice ends the tiled pass and opens a sysmem one, as it does in a
  pass tiled outright; before, the whole pass fell back to its sysmem recording. The random frames hold both
  recordings of that to each other as before (their sums change: more of those passes are tiled).

drawbench, A610 constants, least of 12 frames, us a draw: S 4.75 -> 3.21, K 2.78 -> 2.04, Q 3.47 -> 2.55, U 7.1 -> 6.7.
280 tests, golden three ways, both chips.


---
diff --git a/hakios-metal/include/hakios-metal/command.hpp b/hakios-metal/include/hakios-metal/command.hpp
index a08c155..17f59c9 100644
--- a/hakios-metal/include/hakios-metal/command.hpp
+++ b/hakios-metal/include/hakios-metal/command.hpp
@@ -347,6 +347,9 @@ private:
         // one the pass's draws call for, now that they are known
         bool dual = false;
         pm4::Stream sysStream, headGmem;
+        // (recorded both ways until its draws left no doubt that it is tiled -- render::gmemWorth's answer could no
+        // longer come out sysmem whatever the draws still to come -- and for tiles alone from then on: draw())
+        bool tiledEarly = false;
         uint32_t clears = 0;        // the attachments a GMEM pass clears in its tiles (render::gmemClearWords), and their words
         uint32_t clearWords[kMaxColorOutputs][4] = {};
         uint64_t kind = 0;          // render::tuneKeyOf the pass and its ordinal in the buffer among passes of that kind
diff --git a/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp b/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
index 1ce26fb..4321643 100644
--- a/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
+++ b/hakios-metal/src/render.cpp
@@ -4835,6 +4835,40 @@ bool CommandBuffer::draw(const Program& program, const RenderPass& pass, const D
         open_->cache->cur[1].forget();
     }
     if (timed) drawStamp(uint32_t(2 * (drawsProfiled_.size() - 1) + 1));
+    // A pass recorded both ways is recorded for tiles alone from the draw at which closePass's choice can no longer
+    // come out sysmem: the choice is render::gmemWorth's over what the pass holds, and what it holds only grows --
+    // its draws, the attachments they touch, whether one reads its target -- while what a pass loads and stores is
+    // never more than every attachment it has. CoreAnimation's main pass is a hundred draws and more, tiled every
+    // frame, and each of them was written a second time for a sysmem pass that never ran. (What is on the stream is
+    // what closePass would have put there: the tiles' head now, the tiles when it closes.)
+    if (open_->dual) {
+        bool certain = false;
+        if (gmemOff_ & kGmemByDrawsAlone) {
+            certain = open_->draws >= gmemMinDraws_;
+        } else if (open_->draws >= std::min(gmemMinDraws_, render::kGmemFewDraws)) {
+            if (open_->read != 0) {
+                certain = true;   // (a draw reads its target: tiles)
+            } else {
+                uint64_t touched = 0, all = 0;
+                for (uint32_t i = 0; i < kMaxColorOutputs; i++) {
+                    const Texture* t = i == 0 ? open_->pass.color0 : open_->pass.more[i - 1].texture;
+                    if (t == nullptr) continue;
+                    const uint32_t bytes = t->info().bytesPerPixel;
+                    all += bytes;
+                    if ((gmemOff_ & kGmemEveryAttachment) || (((open_->written | open_->read | open_->clears) >> i) & 1)) touched += bytes;
+                }
+                // (gmemWorth: tiles when draws * 22 touched >= bar * (11 (loaded + stored) - 10 cleared), and that is at
+                // most bar * 22 * every attachment's bytes)
+                certain = touched != 0 && uint64_t(open_->draws) * touched >= uint64_t(gmemMinDraws_) * all;
+            }
+        }
+        if (certain) {
+            appendStream(stream_, open_->headGmem);
+            open_->sysStream.clear();
+            open_->dual = false;
+            open_->tiledEarly = true;
+        }
+    }
     counts_.draws++;
     if ((profile_ || tuning_) && !profiled_.empty()) profiled_.back().draws++;
     // a stage with device buffers may write them (ldib's table is stib's): its whole table is used for writing
@@ -5111,6 +5145,10 @@ void CommandBuffer::closePass() {
             if ((profile_ || tuning_) && !profiled_.empty()) profiled_.back().sysmemWhy = why;
         }
         open_->dual = false;
+    } else if (open_->tiledEarly && !(gmemOff_ & kGmemByDrawsAlone)) {
+        // (tiled for what it holds, decided while it was being recorded: noted as above)
+        noted = std::max(noted, gmemMinDraws_);
+        belowBar = open_->draws < gmemMinDraws_;
     }
     if (open_->kind != 0) queue_.noteDraws(open_->kind, open_->ordinal, noted);
     if (open_->gmem && open_->bodies.size() != 0) {
